From: xPDFSDK team <noreply@xpdfsdk.local>
Date: 2026-06-18
Subject: [PATCH ship-0013] Add a path display-list fast path for Form XObjects

Background
==========
Some PDFs, including the `/Meta20` case from `error.pdf`, wrap tens of
thousands of simple filled path objects inside one Form XObject. PDFium's
normal Form path enters `CPDF_RenderStatus::ProcessForm()` and then replays
the Form through `RenderObjectList()`, paying the full per-object render
dispatch stack for every child path. Progressive rendering does not help this
case because the expensive Form render is one atomic PDFium call with no useful
pause boundary inside the path-heavy Form body.

This patch
==========
1. Adds `core/fpdfapi/render/veloce_path_display_list.{h,cpp}` as a separate
   implementation unit for the native display-list experiment.
2. Adds the default-off `FPDFEX_FEATURE_PATH_DISPLAY_LIST_FORM` feature bit to
   `FPDFEx_RenderCallbacks::feature_flags`.
3. Hooks `CPDF_RenderStatus::ProcessForm()` so eligible Form XObjects can be
   compiled into a compact path display list and replayed into the same
   `CFX_RenderDevice` bitmap.
4. Fails closed: if the Form contains non-path objects, strokes, pattern paint,
   transparency, complex clips, forced-color mode, or an unsupported state, the
   code returns `kNotEligible` before drawing and the original
   `RenderObjectList()` path runs unchanged.
5. Retains `CPDF_Path` values in the path table. `CPDF_Path` is copy-on-write,
   so this keeps the original path data shared instead of deep-copying every
   `CFX_Path` point vector.
6. Checks the existing scoped render cancellation callback every 64 display-list
   nodes during replay.

The initial v1 target is the Meta20-class fill-only path workload. It does not
cache compiled lists across renders yet and it does not replace the general
PDFium renderer.

